        "original_id": "00067e78-377a-53ac-9cab-c13783e85df6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Gorton, Harold Holt, Tony Eggleton, Robert Menzies, John McEwen, William McMahon\n- Roles: Prime Minister of Australia, press secretary\n- Organizations: University of Melbourne, Australian Film Institute Awards\n- Places: Stanmore, New South Wales, Australia\n- Events: 1967 disappearance and death of Harold Holt, 1969 Australian Film Institute Awards\n\nFacts:\n- John Gorton was born on 9 September 1911 and died on 19 May 2002.\n- Harold Holt was born in Stanmore, New South Wales and won a scholarship to study law at the University of Melbourne.\n- Tony Eggleton served as press secretary to Prime Minister Harold Holt at the time of Holt's disappearance and death in December 1967.\n- In 1969, Australian Prime Minister John Gorton hosted the Australian Film Institute Awards ceremony.\n- John Gorton was the 19th Prime Minister of Australia and was a long-serving minister in the governments of Robert Menzies, Harold Holt, John McEwen, and William McMahon.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "e60dd7b9-26ad-5230-875d-574319c8060e",
        "text": "Page: John Gorton. Sentence: Sir John Grey Gorton {'1': \", '2': \", '3': \", '4': \"} (9 September 1911 – 19 May 2002) was the 19th Prime Minister of Australia and long serving minister in the governments of Sir Robert Menzies, Harold Holt, Sir John McEwen and Sir William McMahon.\nPage: Harold Holt. Sentence: He was born in Stanmore, New South Wales and won a scholarship to study law at the University of Melbourne.\nPage: 1969 Australian Film Institute Awards. Sentence: Australian Prime Minister John Gorton hosted the ceremony.\nPage: Tony Eggleton. Sentence: He is best remembered by many Australians as the press secretary to the Prime Minister of Australia, Harold Holt, at the time of the latter's disappearance and death in December 1967.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
